<title>CUBA: Havana film festival honors Mexico's Ripstein.</title>
<headline>Havana film festival honors Mexico's Ripstein.</headline>
<dateline>HAVANA 1996-12-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexican director Arturo Ripstein won the award for best feature film in the annual Havana film festival on Friday for his &quot;Deep Crimson&quot; (&quot;Profundo Carmesi&quot;).</p>
<p>Second prize went to Peru's Francisco Lombardi for &quot;Under the Skin&quot; (&quot;Bajo la Piel&quot;), while Brazilian Rosemberg Cariry took third prize with &quot;Corisco and Dada&quot; (&quot;Corisco y Dada&quot;).</p>
<p>The presentation ceremony was to be held later on Friday, closing the 11-day festival.</p>
</text>
